NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/agent.dedupStateTouching kind=func
  digest=b3:1bfebd52d5d97b12634f8ea2c1bcfa5c9757e406af24f5f022366cdcff51b967 file=neo/internal/agent/agent.go range=2183:2205 lang=go exported=false byte_range=96997:97756
  sig=func dedupStateTouching(calls []llm.ToolCall) []int
  doc=dedupStateTouching returns, for each call index, the index of an EARLIER call\nin the same batch it is an equivalent duplicate of (-1 when it is canonical\nor not a dedup candidate). Only non-idempotent state-touching calls are\ndeduped; independent reversible calls are always -1 so they keep dispatching\nconcurrently. The canonical (first) occurrence runs once and the duplicates\njoin its result.
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/neo/internal/agent/agent.go

